  "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
  "code": "import backtrader as bt\n\n\nclass MacdCrossOneDayHold(bt.Strategy):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.macd = bt.indicators.MACD(\n            self.data, period_me1=12, period_me2=26, period_signal=9\n        )\n        self.crossover = bt.indicators.CrossOver(self.macd.macd, self.macd.signal)\n        self.order = None\n        self.capital = 100.0\n        self.broker.set_coc(True)\n\n    def notify_order(self, order):\n        if order.status in [order.Completed, order.Canceled, order.Margin, order.Rejected]:\n            self.order = None\n\n    def next(self):\n        if self.order:\n            return\n\n        if self.position:\n            open_price = self.data.open[0]\n            close_price = self.data.close[0]\n            self.order = self.close(exectype=bt.Order.Close)\n            self.capital *= (1 + (close_price - open_price) / open_price)\n        else:\n            if self.crossover[0] > 0:\n                self.order = self.buy()",
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "topic": "capital tracking vs. broker cash",
      "choice": "Maintain a separate self.capital float starting at 100.0, updated after each completed trade via the exact stated formula Capital_new = Capital_old * (1 + (close_t+1 - open_t+1)/open_t+1), independent of the harness-fixed $10,000 broker cash.",
      "reason": "The harness fixes cerebro's starting cash at $10,000, which cannot be reconciled with the spec's stated $100 initial capital; the spec's requirement to 'track the capital dynamics' is a formulaic bookkeeping requirement, not a broker cash setting, so it is implemented as its own tracked variable."
    },
    {
      "topic": "order size for actual backtrader trades",
      "choice": "Use plain self.buy() and self.close() with the default fixed-stake sizer (canonical default 1), rather than sizing orders by dollar value of self.capital.",
      "reason": "Since real broker cash ($10,000) and the spec's tracked capital ($100 baseline) are on different scales and cannot be reconciled, a literal value-based order size is not meaningful; per canonical default 1, unresolved sizing falls back to the plain default sizer, while the spec's required capital compounding is still tracked exactly via the dedicated formula-based self.capital variable."
    },
    {
      "topic": "same-day T+1 open entry / T+1 close exit",
      "choice": "Enable cheat-on-close on the broker (self.broker.set_coc(True)) in __init__; submit the entry as a plain Market order (fills at the next bar's open, standard behavior) and the exit as self.close(exectype=bt.Order.Close) (fills at that same bar's close due to COC).",
      "reason": "This is the literal, exact way to realize 'buy at t+1 open, sell at t+1 close, same day' within a single next()-per-bar backtrader strategy; set_coc is a documented broker feature settable from strategy code and is not a deviation from the specified entry/exit prices or timing."
    }
  ],
